meta {
  name: Monday, as it will actually run
  type: http
  seq: 75
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetable-occurrences?branch_id={{branchId}}&date=2026-11-02
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.count: eq 4
  res.body.occurrences: isArray
  res.body.from: eq 2026-11-02
}

docs {
  This is the route a timetable screen, a substitution roster and the register
  all read. It is the plan folded over the calendar and then over the
  deviations: weekly slots become dated occurrences, and each one carries its
  state - planned, relocated, substituted, retimed, cancelled or added.

  Times come from the bell schedule the day's schedule names. Where no bell
  exists for a period the occurrence still appears with start_minute 0,
  end_minute 0 and times_resolved false, so a reader can tell "no bell" from
  "midnight".

  The id on each occurrence is derived, not stored. Nothing is written when
  this is called and there is no occurrences table.

  branch_id is required, and either date, or from and to together. Giving
  date alongside from and to is 400 rather than one silently winning.
}
